  "id": "D3",
  "answer": "In the RAG paper, the difference between RAG-Sequence and RAG-Token is:\n\n- **RAG-Sequence:** Uses the same retrieved document to predict all target tokens in the sequence, treating the retrieved document as a single latent variable that is marginalized [rag_lewis_2020.pdf p.3].\n- **RAG-Token:** Can draw a different latent document for each target token, allowing the generator to combine content from multiple documents when producing an answer [rag_lewis_2020.pdf p.3].",
